# --- Prototyping and third-party reference material -----------------------
# `reference/` holds what this project was DERIVED from or measured against,
# not what it is: Aguet's MATLAB implementation, the paper PDF, exploratory
# notebooks, and the rendered figures from past runs. Kept on disk because
# they are worth re-reading; kept out of git because none of it is source and
# the MATLAB tree alone is ~10 MB of committed binaries (.mex*).
reference/

# --- Data and run artifacts ----------------------------------------------
# The two bead crops in `data/` ARE tracked (39x39 and 62x62 uint16, a few kB
# each) so that `python scripts/run.py` reproduces the README's audit panel out
# of the box. Everything else under data/ is an OUTPUT -- regenerate it:
#     python scripts/localize_movie.py        -> data/hyp7_locs/*.parquet
#     python scripts/run.py --out result.png  -> the audit panel
data/**/*.parquet
data/**/meta.json
data/hyp7_locs/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.nd2
*.czi
!data/beads_60x_still.tif
!data/beads_60x_still_02.tif

# Figures, logs and scratch. `docs/*.md` is tracked; nothing binary is.
*.png
*.pdf
*.log
*.npz
*.pkl
*.mp4
*.out
*.bak
*.ipynb

# The golden fixtures under tests/fixtures/ ARE tracked (~1.6 MB of JSON):
# they are the contract the Rust port is tested against, and CI needs them
# without a Python run. Regenerate with `python scripts/make_fixtures.py`.
